    "case_id": "769",
    "case_summary": "A 29-year-old female presented with a large pelvic mass. Physical examination revealed a soft to firm, large bosselated mass with restricted mobility arising from the pelvis and reaching up to the epigastrium. The patient had primary infertility. The mass was extending from the right adnexa to the left. The patient also had bilateral breast nodules suggestive of fibroadenomas on imaging.\n\nPer abdomen examination: Soft to firm, large bosselated mass with restricted mobility arising from pelvis to epigastrium. Per speculum examination: Cervix not visualized, large firm mass extending into pouch of Douglas. Uterus not felt separately from the mass.\n\n{'Laboratory Tests': 'Serum tumor markers (CA 125, CA 19.9, CEA, AFP, Inhibin and LDH) were within normal limits', 'Imaging Studies': {'MRI': 'Findings were suggestive of an ovarian primary', 'Histopathology': {'Microscopic Findings': 'Spindle cell tumor composed of elongated cells arranged in long sweeping to poorly formed fascicles. Diffuse hemangiopericytomatous pattern of vasculature. Prominent eosinophilic nucleoli with perinucleolar halo.', 'Immunohistochemistry': '- Smooth muscle actin (SMA): Diffusely positive\\n- FH: Global loss of expression\\n- 2-SC: Absence of staining\\n- MIB-1 labeling index: 1-5%'}}, 'Genetic Testing': 'Next generation sequencing (NGS) detected a pathogenic variant in the FH gene (FHc.999C > A p.Cys333Ter)'}",
